  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.553,
            0.048,
            0.861,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The Baudhāyana-Pythagoras Theorem"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.088,
            0.845,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? If (a, b, c) is a Baudhāyana triple, then (ka, kb, kc) is also a Baudhāyana triple where k is any positive integer. Is this statement true?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.131,
            0.847,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This statement can be shown to be true in the same way. Since (a, b, c) is a Baudhāyana triple, we have "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 2 }   + b ^ { 2 } = c ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We need to check whether "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( k a ) ^ { 2 } + ( k b ) ^ { 2 } = \\tilde { ( k c ) ^ { 2 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.271,
            0.19,
            0.725,
            0.211
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "(ka)^{2}=ka\\times ka=k^{2} a^{2}, \\text { and } (kb)^{2}=kb\\times kb=k^{2} b^{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.358,
            0.216,
            0.637,
            0.237
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{S}0,(ka)^{2}+(kb)^{2}=k^{2}a^{2}+k^{2}b^{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.242,
            0.541,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Taking out the common factor, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.385,
            0.265,
            0.611,
            0.285
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "( k a ) ^ { 2 } + ( k b ) ^ { 2 } = k ^ { 2 }   ( a ^ { 2 } + b ^ { 2 } ) ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.289,
            0.402,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 2 } + b ^ { 2 } = c ^ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.377,
            0.313,
            0.62,
            0.332
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "(ka)^{2}+(kb)^{2}=k^{2}\\ c^{2}=(kc)^{2}."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.338,
            0.846,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, (ka, kb, kc) is a Baudhāyana triple if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( a ,   b ,   c )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a Baudhāyana triple. We call "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( k a , k b , k c )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "scaled version",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( a , b , c )"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.379,
            0.846,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Baudhāyana triple that does not have any common factor greater than 1 is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "primitive Baudhāyana triple",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". So, (3, 4, 5) is primitive, whereas (9,12,15) is not."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.443,
            0.845,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Is (5, 12, 13) a primitive Baudhāyana triple? What are the other primitive Baudhāyana triples with numbers less than or equal to 20?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.495,
            0.846,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Generate 5 scaled versions of each of these primitive triples. Are these scaled versions primitive?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.547,
            0.847,
            0.619
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ If (a, b, c) is non-primitive, and the integers have f — greater than 1 — as a common factor, then is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( \\frac{a}{f}, \\frac{b}{f}, \\frac{c}{f} \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " a Baudhāyana triple? Check this statement for (9, 12, 15). Justify this statement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.622,
            0.845,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we can find all the primitive triples, we can find all the Baudhāyana triples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.668,
            0.586,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How do we generate more primitive triples?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.693,
            0.845,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know the relation between the sum of consecutive odd numbers and square numbers."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.437,
            0.729,
            0.563,
            0.785
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{array} { c } { 1 = 1 ^ { 2 } } \\\\ { 1 + 3 = 2 ^ { 2 } } \\\\ { 1 + 3 + 5 = 3 ^ { 2 } } \\end{array}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.789,
            0.845,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The sum of the first n odd numbers is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { 2 } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let us express this algebraically."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.816,
            0.718,
            0.861
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For this, we need to know the nth odd number. What is it? The nth odd number is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 n - 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.273,
            0.865,
            0.674,
            0.912
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_16_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "\\underbrace{1+3+5+\\cdots+(2n-3)}_{ Sum of first   (n-1)   odd numbers } + \\underbrace{n^2}_{}"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.874,
            0.914,
            0.911,
            0.934
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "49"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
